    <item>
      <title>Squeak 2.27.2</title>
      <pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 04:08:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22702</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.27.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>Settings › Extensions no longer says "Not in this build" for Claude Code (external), Codex (external) and RasanAI: an add-on is unavailable only when the daemon says so, not when the app has no page for it.</li><li>"Download automatically" is now off by default: Squeak checks for updates on its own but asks before downloading. Installs that had it switched on by an earlier version are reset once; turn it on again in Settings, About if you want it.</li><li>A message sent while the agent is working (or a pond member's) now waits in the chat itself, dimmed under its author at the end of the transcript, with Steer, Edit and Remove; when its turn starts, that same row becomes the prompt in place, with no second row and no jump. The stack above the composer no longer repeats it (a small "N queued" note stays when two or more wait).</li><li>Fixed a message sent while the agent was working showing twice, once solid and once dimmed: the host now keeps the send's id with the queued or steered message, so the dimmed row always becomes the real one.</li><li>File tabs are remembered: the files you had open in a stream come back after a relaunch, in the order you opened them among the threads, if the file still exists.</li><li>Switching a Markdown file between Preview and Source keeps your place instead of jumping to the top.</li><li>You can see what is working at a glance: a folded or open pond shows the working glyph where its count sits when any thread inside is working, the needs-you count (wins over working) or an error mark; the count returns when it is quiet.</li><li>Streams use a new dot-grid glyph instead of the three waves: still and dim when idle, a soft brightness wave while a thread works, steady amber for needs you and red for an error. It holds one frame under Reduce Motion, and VoiceOver reads "greenroom, 1 working, 1 needs you".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.1</h4><ul><li>A chat no longer says "very large" because its transcript file is big: the notice and the context popover now follow what is actually sent, and the popover says where the chat compacts ("Compacts automatically at 200k tokens"). Over that point the notice reads "Compacting soon to keep replies fast".</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.27.0</h4><ul><li>New setting in Account: "Keep recent chats in Squeak's cloud (encrypted)", on by default once you are signed in. Your iPhone and browser can then open your last 30 days of chats while this Mac sleeps, or on a new device. The copy is sealed with your key, so Squeak can't read it; turning the setting off deletes it.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
